<script type="application/ld+json" is:inline>{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","@id":"https://nbasalaries.com/teams/dallas-mavericks/#faq","isPartOf":{"@id":"https://nbasalaries.com/teams/dallas-mavericks/"},"mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Who is the highest-paid player on the Dallas Mavericks?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Kyrie Irving has the largest current cap hit at $39,491,282. His listed cash salary is $39,491,282."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the Dallas Mavericks payroll?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The active roster cap payroll is $177,194,562 for 2026–27 in the 2026-10-21 snapshot. Dead cap and cap holds are separate."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How much of the salary cap does the roster use?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Standard-roster cap charges equal 107.42% of the NBA’s $164,961,000 salary cap. This can exceed 100% because NBA rules allow certain exceptions."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Are future contract totals fully guaranteed?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. Scheduled years can include player options, team options and conditional protection. The contract table identifies options where confirmed."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Why are salary and cap hit different?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Incentives, contract rules and minimum-salary adjustments can make a player’s cash pay differ from the amount charged to the team’s salary cap."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How Much Have the Mavericks Spent Each Season?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Track Dallas Mavericks payroll in dollars and as a share of the league’s salary cap. Comparing cap share helps put different seasons on the same scale. Swipe Left or Right to Explore Seasons Tap the Graph for Details Tap or hover a season for its details. Past seasons use historical cap payroll; 2026–27 is the current active roster plus dead cap. Future transactions can change the current-season figure."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Where Do the Mavericks Sit Against the Salary Cap?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Dallas Mavericks salaries add up to a cap payroll of $189.07 million for 2026–27, $24.11 million above the $164.96 million salary cap. That figure includes $11.87 million in dead cap on top of a standard roster of $177.19 million. Kyrie Irving tops the payroll at $39.49 million, ahead of P.J. Washington on $19.81 million and Daniel Gafford on $17.26 million, together about 43.2% of the roster total. Their tax salary is $11.10 million below the $200.43 million luxury-tax line and apron salary sits $18.34 million under the $209.02 million first apron. The Dallas Mavericks standard roster accounts for $177.19M. Add $11.87M in dead cap to reach $189.07M before cap holds. Holds are separate accounting charges, not signed salary payments."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What does going over the tax line mean?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The luxury tax is an additional team expense. It rises in bands as tax salary moves above the threshold; teams with a recent history of paying tax can face higher repeater rates. The final bill depends on the season-end calculation."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Where Does the Mavericks’ Payroll Rank in the NBA?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Dallas Mavericks rank #23 of 30 by 2026–27 cap payroll. Each bar is drawn to scale, and the change compares with the same measure for 2025–26."}}]}</script>
